# init removes the always-loaded block an older CLI wrote — both on a first
# init over a stale CLAUDE.md and on a re-init — and never writes one.

env CONSTITUTION_TODAY=2026-07-02

# first init: CLAUDE.md held only the block, so it is deleted
exec constitution init
stdout '^constitution: removed CLAUDE.md, which held only the always-loaded constitution block$'
! exists CLAUDE.md
! exists AGENTS.md

# re-init over a block appended to user content: only the block goes
cp legacy-agents.md AGENTS.md
exec constitution init
stdout '^constitution: removed the always-loaded constitution block from AGENTS.md$'
cmp AGENTS.md want-agents.md
! exists CLAUDE.md

-- CLAUDE.md --
<!-- BEGIN adr-sourced-constitution v1 (managed — do not edit by hand; `constitution init` updates it) -->
@constitution/constitution.md
<!-- END adr-sourced-constitution v1 -->
-- legacy-agents.md --
# Agents

Run the tests.

<!-- BEGIN adr-sourced-constitution v1 (managed — do not edit by hand; `constitution init` updates it) -->
Before planning, read `constitution/constitution.md`; it is this project's governing constitution and takes precedence over inferred conventions.
<!-- END adr-sourced-constitution v1 -->
-- want-agents.md --
# Agents

Run the tests.
